---
description: Oracle SQL migrations — forward-only, snake_case
globs: sql/**/*.sql,db/**/*.sql
alwaysApply: false
---

# Data & Migrations

- Tables: `snake_case` plural (e.g. `tasks`, `appointments`, `notifications`).
- Files: numbered forward-only SQL under `sql/` (e.g. `V001__create_tasks.sql`).
- Every schema change = new file — never edit a migration already applied.
- Parameterize app queries via `executeQuery` binds — not string concatenation.
- PHI-adjacent columns: comment in SQL for future encryption review.
- Appointment/notification rows: include `created_at`; notifications include `channel`, `status`, `sent_at`.
